Here's a PHP script that takes user input and a specific character as arguments and returns the number of times that character appears in the input string:

<?php 

if(isset($_POST['submit'])){

  // get the user input string and character
  $input = $_POST['input_string'];
  $character = $_POST['input_character'];

  // initialize count variable
  $count = 0;

  // loop through the input string and count the number of occurrences of the character
  for($i = 0; $i < strlen($input); $i++){
    if($input[$i] == $character){
      $count++;
    }
  }

  // print the output
  echo "The character '$character' appears $count times in the input string '$input'.";

}

?>

